{"component_id_namespace":"ec077a53-0b40-5f21-b1fe-a62094d2476b","component_schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","components":[{"attributes":{"code":"TMC","legacy_node_id":"ks-topeka:tmc:2.40.180","page_type":"section"},"citation":"2.40.180","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/2.40.180","content_hash":"9767ffcaba0ff4310a8617ac37e2dc4b8f7bb5ac3ea2e93bf237dc1c68366dcb","heading":"Notice to appear – Contents – Form.","ordinal":0,"parent_source_component_key":null,"schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:2.40.180:section","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/2.40.180","text":"(a) A notice to appear shall describe the offense charged, shall summon the accused person to appear, shall contain a space in which the accused person may agree, in writing, to appear at a time not less than five days after such notice to appear is given, unless the accused person shall demand an earlier hearing. A notice to appear may be signed by a Municipal Judge, the clerk of the Municipal Court, the City Attorney, an Assistant City Attorney, a law enforcement officer of the City, an animal control officer, or a Fire Department employee with authority to enforce the Uniform Fire Code.\n(b) If the accused person is a legal entity, the notice to appear shall summon an agent.\n(c) A notice to appear shall be deemed sufficient if in substantially the form of the notice to appear set out in K.S.A. 12-4204 and amendments thereto, or if in substantially the following form:\nIN THE MUNICIPAL COURT OF TOPEKA, KANSAS\nThe City of Topeka, Kansas vs. ________________________________, (Accused person) ________________________________, (Address)\nNOTICE TO APPEAR\nThe City of Topeka, Kansas, To The Above Named Accused Person.\nYou are hereby summoned to appear before the Municipal Court of Topeka, Kansas, on the ________ day of ________, ________, at ___________ o’clock, ________.m., to answer a complaint charging you with\n_________________________________\n_________________________________\n________________________________.\nIf you fail to appear a warrant will be issued for your arrest.\nDated __________________, ________.\n_________________________________\n/s/____________________ Signature of Official\n/s/____________________ Title of Official\nI agree to appear in said Court at said time and place.\n_________________________________\n/s/_________________________ Signature of Accused Person\nRETURN\nThe undersigned hereby certifies that on the _____________ day of ___________, ________, the notice to appear was served, mailed or delivered.\n/s/________________________ Signature and Title of Official\n(Ord. 20383 § 3, 11-1-22. Formerly 2.110.180.)\nCross References: Fire Department, TMC 2.20.030 ; City Attorney, TMC 2.20.070 ; Police Department, TMC 2.20.090 ; animal control officer, TMC 6.05.040 .\nState Law References: Similar State statute, K.S.A. 12-4204 .","type":"section","workbench_component_id":"c07133cd-f57f-5812-979f-05a05f655068"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"2.40.180","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/2.40.180","content_hash":"6c96fe886ddafeb78f25f45ac1ba6e4499879cb90c91548928b8c012b00d204a","heading":null,"ordinal":0,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:2.40.180:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:2.40.180:block:0","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/2.40.180","text":"(a) A notice to appear shall describe the offense charged, shall summon the accused person to appear, shall contain a space in which the accused person may agree, in writing, to appear at a time not less than five days after such notice to appear is given, unless the accused person shall demand an earlier hearing. A notice to appear may be signed by a Municipal Judge, the clerk of the Municipal Court, the City Attorney, an Assistant City Attorney, a law enforcement officer of the City, an animal control officer, or a Fire Department employee with authority to enforce the Uniform Fire Code.","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"9182776f-64a7-59fb-8466-8b4ac5baa19e"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"2.40.180","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/2.40.180","content_hash":"2a980f66edd6ddea4ce978204ff681c021bf5747d26446908bbb6bcd335fbaef","heading":null,"ordinal":1,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:2.40.180:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:2.40.180:block:1","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/2.40.180","text":"(b) If the accused person is a legal entity, the notice to appear shall summon an agent.","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"86deb924-11f0-5f3a-b89f-1ba95ec157fe"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"2.40.180","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/2.40.180","content_hash":"7e09e725f264a0b1a9d34ed921d583d8f019ba09dd7da9e7c05de93e8ed3d502","heading":null,"ordinal":2,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:2.40.180:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:2.40.180:block:2","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/2.40.180","text":"(c) A notice to appear shall be deemed sufficient if in substantially the form of the notice to appear set out in K.S.A. 12-4204 and amendments thereto, or if in substantially the following form:","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"1de3be45-236d-54bc-ad56-21cd9954dcaf"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"2.40.180","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/2.40.180","content_hash":"cba1edc1a1cfbc8f41c1298ced8da406d84edbe74cf9b79127f2fb2fcd1c8f77","heading":null,"ordinal":3,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:2.40.180:section","schem